    {
      "dom_id": "question-85924",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "Let $A$ be a $3\\times 3$ matrix with the characteristic polynomial $p(\\lambda )={\\lambda }^{3}-{\\lambda }^{2}+3\\lambda -16.$ Then, ${A}^{3}=$",
      "worked_solution": "Using the Cayley-Hamilton theorem, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p(A) & =O \\\\ {A}^{3}-{A}^{2}+3A-16I & =O \\\\ {A}^{3} & ={A}^{2}-3A+16I.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
